        "responses": {
          "values": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "=You classify a WhatsApp message into exactly one JSON object. Return ONLY\nvalid JSON, no other text, no markdown fences.\n\nCurrent date/time (PKT): {{ $now.setZone('Asia/Karachi').toFormat(\"EEEE, dd LLL yyyy HH:mm\") }}\n\nPending tasks (row_number | Course Name | Assigned Task | Date):\n{{ $json.pendingTasksAsText }}\nDecide intent:\n- \"new_task\": message describes one or more new assignments/quizzes/projects\n  with due dates\n- \"submission_update\": message indicates something was turned in\n- \"query\": the user is asking a question about their deadlines (e.g. \"what's\n  due this week?\", \"when's my stats quiz?\") rather than adding a task or\n  reporting a submission\n- \"unclear\": none of the above fit confidently, or a submission_update can't\n  be matched to exactly one pending task\n\nFor new_task, return:\n{\n  \"intent\": \"new_task\",\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"assigned_task\": \"Assignment\" | \"Quiz\" | \"Project\" | \"Presentation\" | \"Lab\" | \"Capstone\" | \"Exam\" | \"Paper\" | \"Report\" |,\n      \"course_name\": \"string\",\n      \"date\": \"ISO 8601 in Asia/Karachi, default 23:59 if no time given\",\n      \"guidelines\": \"string, empty if none\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nIf the task type doesn't clearly match any of these, default to Assignment, default course name to 'Task to-do', and note the actual type in Guidelines.\nIf the message describes multiple tasks (e.g. several courses sharing one due date, or a list of separate deadlines), include one object per task in the array.\n\n\nFor submission_update, return:\n{\n  \"intent\": \"submission_update\",\n  \"matched_row_numbers\": [<row_number>, <row_number>, ...],\n  \"matched_summary\": \"e.g. GenAI Assignment 1, Stats Quiz 2\"\n}\n\nMatching rules, in order:\n1. If the message means \"everything\" (e.g. \"all done\", \"everything submitted\",\n   \"finished all of it\"), include the row_number of every pending task in\n   the list above.\n2. If the message specifies a task TYPE only (e.g. \"all assignments done\",\n   \"finished my quizzes\", \"all projects submitted\"), include the row_number\n   of every pending task whose Assigned Task matches that type — ignore\n   tasks of other types even if pending.\n3. If the message names a specific course or task (e.g. \"submitted the\n   genai one\"), match by name as before. If it matches more than one\n   pending task ambiguously, return intent \"unclear\" instead and ask which.\n4. If the message gives no name or type at all (e.g. just \"submitted\" or\n   \"done\"), include only the single soonest-due pending task's row_number.\n\nFor query, return:\n{\n  \"intent\": \"query\",\n  \"reply_text\": \"a natural, WhatsApp-style answer based on the pending tasks\n                  list above\"\n}\n\nFor unclear, return:\n{\n  \"intent\": \"unclear\",\n  \"reply_text\": \"a short WhatsApp-style clarifying question\"\n}"
            },
            {
              "content": "={{ $json.incomingMessage }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {
          "textFormat": {
            "textOptions": {
              "type": "json_object"
            }
          }
        }
      },
